  clock: 3  # 1360
  nonce: '1360'  # 1360
  message: "Fixed in PR #3396 (commit 1824a4cf8). Five extended1 analyzers (luau / smithy / hack / jsonnet / apex) updated to use the established mainstream 5-part dst id shape ({lang}:unresolved:0-0:{name}:unresolved) instead of the legacy 2-part 'unresolved:{name}'. Each existing test_unresolved_call_* test gained an assertion that the dst splits into 5 colon-parts with the expected language token in slot 0; jsonnet adds a fresh test_unresolved_call_dst_is_well_formed_5part_id. 100% coverage on changed files. Out-of-scope follow-up (filed conceptually but not yet a tracker item — could be added if it surfaces): six other analyzers (robot/racket/purescript/scheme/matlab/prisma) emit a 3-part {lang}:unresolved:{name} shape that produces correct language={lang} but malformed boundary-node name/kind slots. Cohort verification: language='unresolved' nodes will drop to 0 on alertmanager (was 39) once the next cohort re-runs."  # 1360
